## Thinking
Both Qwen templates support it (default open `<think>`; `enable_thinking=false` appends an empty think block).
Marin's chat layer (`crates/chat/src/qwen3.rs`, `NO_THINKING`) always renders non-thinking, matching HF for that mode.
Thinking is therefore not reachable through chat, serve or code; it was run by rendering the official template here and
passing it to `marin-run -p` (Qwen3.5: `<think>\n` after the assistant marker; Qwen3: nothing after it).

## Results
Held-out (17 single-shot tasks, frozen before the run; per-task rows in 21-harness/runs/grades.txt):
4b-nothink 13/17, 4b-think 12/17, 17b-nothink 8/17, 17b-think 9/17 (see BENCHMARKS.md for the breakdown).
Manual grades (21-harness/runs/manual.json): all 16 lookup answers correct (17b says `None` for `Ok(None)`: accepted);
E2 4B-non-thinking fail (host mark right, then claims the mark is unusable), 4B-thinking pass, both 1.7B fail;
E3 4B-non-thinking pass, 4B-thinking cut at 2,048 tokens, both 1.7B fail (invent parallel chunks).
LC2 failed everywhere (truth order 257; 4B non-thinking said 076, the second highest bolt price).
Tool format, strict, no repair: 4B non-thinking 2/4 right (TC4 and TC6 wrote `<path>`/rambled), 4B thinking 1/4, 1.7B 0/4
(wrote `<parameter=retry_limit>`, missing closing tags). Dev set (8 tasks, used to fix the harness only): 4B non-thinking 4/8, thinking 5/8.
Repository navigation, 25 tasks via `marin code` (4B, non-thinking, current tree, graded against the code): 15 pass;
dev 9/17, held-out 6/8 (earlier run: 16/25, 9/17 and 7/8). Fails: t2, b5 (ran out of rounds), a2 (call site), a3 (said the
first Ctrl-C is ignored), a5 (wrong condition), a7 (README example, truth 4096), a9, a11, a12, b4. 76 tool calls, 10 invalid,
17 repaired, 3 failed; median 26.8 s, 216,923 prompt tokens, 9,329 written. Thinking was not run here: it is not exposed.
Cost: load 2.4-3.7 s per process; peak process RSS 857-937 MB; GPU 5.97-6.38 GB (all programs, incl. about 0.8 GB desktop).
Cold-process prefill is 134 tok/s for the 4B (12 s for 1.6k tokens) and about 1,100 tok/s for the 1.7B.

## Gates
Q1 (thinking 4B vs 4B): 12 vs 13, median 25.2 vs 11.2 s: FAIL. Q1 for the 1.7B: FAIL (8 and 9).
Q2 (1.7B for light work): lookup+chat 6/8 vs 8/8 = 0.75 < 0.8, and 4.8 s vs 6.0 s = 0.8x > 0.6x: FAIL.
R1: 4B and 1.7B pass; T1: no configuration has 0 malformed calls, including the baseline (so the client keeps repair).
Decision: V10 automatic routing NO-GO. Differences under 3 tasks (n=17) are noise.
Limits: small n; one greedy run per task; the explanation and lookup tasks are drawn from this repository; LC2 and
the tool tasks use a shared prompt that was taught to the 4B only (the 1.7B does not use this XML form natively).
